

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 10

                                  FOR

                                GIOVANNA







          Alberto Clerici
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  Elizabeth I, Queen of England, to her subjects in 1601:
  "You have had, and may have, many mightier and wiser princes sitting upon 
this throne; yet you never had, nor shall have any that will love you 
better."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Winter melted into spring.  Giovanna was resurrected by the spell cast by 
Hakim.  His experience improved his skill in White Magic.
  Maicuru was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Maicuru.  
Sageleaf was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Sageleaf.  
Giovanna rehearsed and practiced her Tactics and improved noticeably.  She 
took her men on military exercises and the 186th Legion rose in quality.
  Tigerhome was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Tigerhome.
  In early summer, Giovanna approached the Monastery with every intention of 
prevailing over it and whatever vile guardian beast lay within.  Giovanna 
encountered the Witch.  Her powers magnified by the Monastery, a White Magic 
Place of Power, chanting her words of magic with breathless precision, 
Giovanna let fly a Spiritwrack spell, to make the Witch quake and shiver 
with spiritual convulsions.
  The Witch cautiously advanced to bow range.  Her powers enhanced by the 
Monastery, a White Magic Place of Power, incanting a Holy Symbol spell, 
Giovanna channelled glowing, interlacing strands of magic.  A golden mist in 
the shape of a cross formed around Giovanna.
  The Witch closed to melee range, filled with maniacal blood-lust.  
The Witch flamboyantly vaulted over Giovanna and contemptuously slashed at 
her but her aim was just off the mark.  Giovanna could not cast a 
Resurrection spell because Giovanna had already cast her allowed number of 
White Magic spells.
  Giovanna energetically thrust at the Witch but her aim was slightly off.  
The Witch slashed at Giovanna with all her strength and would have struck 
Giovanna if Giovanna hadn't ducked just then.  The Witch assailed Giovanna 
and missed.  Giovanna audaciously thrust at the Witch and scored on 
the Witch, inflicting 8 points of damage.  Giovanna feinted one way, then 
crossed over and swang at the Witch and inflicted 4 damage points.  
The Witch was fatally wounded.  Giovanna turned her attention to the hoard 
of the Witch.  Giovanna walked over to a pile of treasure and secured the 
Dome of Opacity.  Giovanna examined the Dome of Opacity and discovered the 
following properties:
  The Dome of Opacity enables you to cast the Hide Feature spell of the 
college of Illusory Magic.  There is a certain number of charges in this 
item, and each time you cast the spell you use up a charge.  When all 
charges are used up, the item becomes useless.  The spell normally will take 
effect as if a magician with a skill level of 2 had cast the spell.
  Giovanna secured the Sword Excalibur.  She examined the Sword Excalibur 
and discovered the following properties:
  Excalibur has a +25% chance to hit and does +4 damage.  In addition, it 
confers extraordinary powers of leadership over members of the human race:  
any human army following a leader who wields Excalibur has its quality 
increased by 1 level.  Green armies become Average, Crack armies become 
Elite and so on.
  Giovanna found 6 gold in the hoard of the Witch.
  Giovanna saw nothing special while scouting out the Monastery.
  Hakim's attempted cast of the Phantasmal Armies spell was unsuccessful.  
Bam Yanga was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Bam Yanga.
  In late summer, her powers magnified by the Monastery, a White Magic Place 
of Power, Giovanna cast a Bless spell.  Pearlgate was magically blessed and 
prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in Pearlgate.
  Kajaani was hit by a plague.  Hakim cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and 
illusory armies were formed for Giovanna.

  In Bam Yanga, Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) brought to bay the 
forces of Giovanna.  Kari (#81)'s forces encountered little resistance in 
Bam Yanga and Kari there established our rule.  Kari leads approximately 1 
Trolls.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) 
invaded Sageleaf, hoping to conquer that province ruled by Giovanna and made 
up of extensive Forests.  Alaric (#22)'s armies took possession of Sageleaf 
practically uncontested.  Alaric leads approximately 1 Bowmen, 3 Legion and 1
Light Cavalry.
  The summer mellowed into fall.  Giovanna gathered her courage and 
nervously entered the Pyramid.  Giovanna drew out her Sword Excalibur.  She 
encountered the Lich.  Uttering her words of magic with trained precision, 
Giovanna let go a Spiritwrack spell, to make the Lich quake and shiver with 
spiritual convulsions.   but the spell seemed ineffective against the Lich.  
Raising its hands high in the air, the Lich cast a Hand Of Death spell and 
began making squeezing motions with its hands.  Giovanna's spell was 
disrupted by the event.  The Lich brought its hands together and yanked them 
apart in a ripping motion, provoking a squeal of pain from Giovanna and 
scored on her, doing 2 points of damage.
  Giovanna advanced to bow range.
  Giovanna charged into the melee.  The Lich curled its phantasmal hand 
around Giovanna's liver and squeezed it and inflicted 2 damage points.  
Giovanna immediately thrust at the Lich and damaged the Lich, inflicting 13 
damage points.  The Lich's spell was disrupted by the event.  The Lich 
lunged at Giovanna but its deathly touch whiffed through the air.
  Hoping to take advantage of a gap in Giovanna's protection, the Lich 
deftly groped for Giovanna but its aim was slightly off.  Giovanna thrust at 
her vaunted enemy and inflicted 12 damage points on the Lich.  Giovanna 
maneuvered for a good attacking position.  Then Giovanna swang at the Lich 
and walloped the Lich with 12 damage points.  The Lich fell, mortally 
injured.  Giovanna looked with satisfaction at the remains of the Lich.  
Giovanna walked over to a mound of treasure and bagged the Reflector of 
Armies.  Giovanna examined the Reflector of Armies and discovered the 
following properties:
  The Reflector of Armies enables you to cast the Phantasmal Armies spell of 
the college of Illusory Magic.  There is a certain number of charges in this 
item, and each time you cast the spell you use up a charge.  When all 
charges are used up, the item becomes useless.  The spell normally will take 
effect as if a magician with a skill level of 2 had cast the spell.
  Giovanna looted 6 gold from the treasure of the Lich.
  While scouting the Pyramid, Giovanna saw a Pentagram which seemed to be of 
a magical nature.
  Magic runes formed on the Pentagram, saying "The Pentagram will try to 
increase your skill in Element Magic by 1 point per visit, up to a maximum 
of 4.  If you have low aptitude, your chance of success is halved for every 
aptitude-level you are deficient in Element Magic.  You must pay 10 gold 
each time the Pentagram is used (to show that you accept these terms, a 
character must give two Scout orders when he Searches this feature.)"

  A great host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Plain province of 
Chandrapur, held by Giovanna.  Chandrapur was overrun and occupied by Teleko 
(#72)'s host.  Teleko leads approximately 2 Dragons, 4 Eagles and 2 Trolls.
  The fall cooled into the stillness of early winter.  Giovanna boldly 
marched her command into Kajaani (#1603).

  The Plain terrain of Kajaani was magically made to appear as Forest.
  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)ian 
empire marched on the Plain province of Kajaani, a land garrisoned by the 
soldiers of Giovanna.  Guerin (#18) commanded the invading armies.  The 
defenders were commanded by Giovanna.  The armies were drawn up into lines 
of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Kajaani (1603):

