  DEFENDING ARMY

  Guerin marched with his loyal troops, eyes set in terrible determination.  
Giovanna led her armies into the fray.  Rolando stood ready at the head of 
his thousands.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  The army of Giovanna used magic to aid their cause.  
Magical phantasmal armies fought with hers soldiers.  Giovanna drew out her 
Sword Excalibur.  She stepped forward and challenged Guerin (#18) to 
honorable combat.  Guerin declined to enter combat.
  The forces commanded by Guerin were disappointed by his faint-heartedness. 
They steadfastly marched on, though with shaken confidence.  Guerin allowed 
a prisoner to believe that allies would soon come to double his forces, then 
gave him a chance to escape.  The prisoner reported the grim news to 
Giovanna, and Giovanna deployed her forces with too much caution.  As the 
fierce battle developed, the tactical abilities of Giovanna and Guerin 
appeared well matched.
  Giovanna waved her Sword Excalibur and her Humans were virtually 
hypnotized!  The Elves commanded by Giovanna were not impressed by her lack 
of leadership ability.
  Out on the right outside wing, the Elite 240th Skeletal Bowmen were 
encouraged to fanatiscm by Guerin, their revered First Elder of Elvenkind.  
They faced the Veteran 275th Legion, who sang out their fiery battle hymns, 
infused with a spirit of righteous, fanatical elan by their exalted King.  
The 124th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 311th Legion and attacked them.  
In this sector, the 240th Skeletal Bowmen's commander led his troops badly 
because he had drunk all through that night, not having expected a battle on 
the morrow.  The 240th Skeletal Bowmen battled the 275th Legion and were 
bent back by their pressure.
  Within the interior front, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen were arrayed 
against the Veteran 274th Legion, who sang their thunderous battle hymns, 
inspired with a spirit of fanatical elan by their exalted King.  In this 
match, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen launched their catapult missiles before the 
enemy had fully arrived.  These attacks staggered them with telling blows.  
In spite of the 108th Skeletal Bowmen's good fortune, the 108th Skeletal 
Bowmen battled the 274th Legion and could not quite hold their ground 
against their determined opponent.
  In the interior lines, the Crack 110th Bowmen were encouraged to berserk 
fanatiscm by Guerin, their revered First Elder of Elvenkind.  They faced the 
Veteran 186th Legion, who sang their heroic ballads, inspired with a spirit 
of fanatical fury by their exalted King.  In this match, the men of the 
110th Bowmen ran into some treacherous footing and were afflicted with great 
disruption.  It seemed probable that the 186th Legion would break through 
and win.
  The battle blazed with a terrible fury.  The 186th Legion became 
disorganized when they ran into a stray herd of buffaloes, putting them at a 
severe disadvantage.  Even so, the 110th Bowmen battled with the 186th 
Legion and gradually gave ground.
  Within the interior lines, the 20th Legion faced the 177th Legion, who 
sang their fiery heroic ballads, infused with a righteous, fanatical elan by 
their exalted King.  Here, the morale of the soldiers of the 20th Legion 
were uplifted when one sergeant yelled "Let's win one for the King!"  , and 
the battle cry was taken up by all the men of the 20th Legion.  Even with 
the 20th Legion's good fortune, the 20th Legion battled the 177th Legion and 
was forced to retreat in disorder.
  In the interior lines, the 230th Legion were arrayed against the Elite 
259th Legion, who were aided by a Thunderbird who flew down from the heavens 
to aid their righteous Heavenly cause, and were inspired to fanaticism by 
its divine splendor.  The 277th Eagles swooped down on the 331st Bowmen and 
attacked without mercy.  The 277th Eagles were bothered by the fire of their 
feared Bowmen enemy.  The 230th Legion fought with the 259th Legion and were 
beaten down like overripe pumpkins.
  On the left flank, the Elite 241st Skeletal Bowmen faced the 299th Legion. 
In this engagement, the 299th Legion bravely charged their enemy, but became 
strung out and were thrown back by a well-timed, sustained countercharge.  
The 241st Skeletal Bowmen battled with the 299th Legion and the fighting 
here was inconclusive.
  The battle ended victoriously for the soldiers of Giovanna as they broke 
through at a critical moment.  The 177th Legion scattered the 20th Legion in 
all directions.  The 259th Legion slew the 230th Legion almost to a man.  
The 331st Bowmen demolished the 277th Eagles.  The 311th Legion overtook the 
enemy in their panicky retreat and were driven off by the 108th Skeletal 
Bowmen in a tough rearguard battle.  The 242nd Light Cavalry chased after 
the enemy and annihilated the 74th Camel Corps.  The 185th Light Cavalry 
pursued the enemy and were beaten off by the 241st Skeletal Bowmen after a 
tough rearguard action.  The 243rd Light Cavalry gave chase and were beaten 
off by the 110th Bowmen in a tough rearguard battle.  The 215th Camel Corps 
overtook the enemy and were beaten off by the 241st Skeletal Bowmen after a 
tough rearguard battle.
  The host of the attacking Kingdom was defeated and forced out of Kajaani.  
The battle affected the quality of our forces:  the fun head-bashing by the 
274th Legion during the battle has elevated the spirits of its warriors, and 
it has achieved Crack quality.  We could not have been better satisfied with 
the fighting spirit of the 186th Legion, and we have raised its rating to 
Crack.  The 21st Legion was tested during the battle and came through with a 
good effort.  We can now rank it an Average unit.  Guerin pulled back to 
Rejaf with his command.

  A host of savage warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Desert province of Jaguardo,
held by Giovanna.  Teleko (#72)'s forces took Jaguardo without any major 
battles.  Teleko leads approximately 2 Dragons, 5 Eagles and 1 Trolls.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) invaded the province of Tigerhome, a 
Forest area owned by Giovanna.  Tigerhome was conquered and occupied by 
Alaric (#22)'s host.  Alaric leads approximately 1 Bowmen, 3 Legion and 1 
Light Cavalry.
  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Mugai (#3) (whose 
alliances are too incompatible) and Giovanna, degrading their diplomatic 
relations 1 level(s)!
  Giovanna was visited by a hero from Valhalla, named Kurator!  The 
characteristics for this great King from Game 59 are given in your 
"CHARACTERS" report.
  If Kurator searches a feature, any monetary treasure Kurator captures will 
be given to you.  If Kurator captures a magic treasure, Kurator will give it 
to your King when he departs for Valhalla, or you can order Kurator to Give 
it to one of your characters.  You can do anything you want with the magic 
item Kurator came with, but the item will leave at the end of his stay with 
you.  Except for the rules given in this paragraph, Kurator can generally be 
treated just like your other Heroes, and can be affected by any spell except 
Resurrection.  The main limitation in using Kurator is that Kurator has only 
enough patience to practice with you for one of the phase(s) Kurator is with 
you.  Kurator will leave at the end of the last phase Kurator is scheduled 
to serve you, after all battles have been fought.  Kurator can lead armies, 
but when Kurator returns to Valhalla, the armies will normally be left 
leaderless in the province they are in.  If Kurator has the armies in a 
province you don't own, they will be transferred to your lowest-numbered 
leader in the same province, or at last resort, the garrison commander in an 
adjacent province owned by you.  If no leader is available, the armies will 
be disbanded.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Giovanna for this year.


  Giovanna treated with her ally Bradipo I (#2).  Giovanna proposed a treaty 
with Mugai (#3)'s Kingdom, and the magnanimous offer was accepted.  May the 
treaty between Giovanna and Cosmic Herderer Mugai last forever!
  Giovanna treated with her ally Hokuto (#4).  Giovanna treated with her 
ally Prometeo (#5).  Giovanna treated with her ally II Kahn (#6).  Giovanna 
treated with her ally Circe (#8).  Giovanna treated with her ally Agesilao 
(#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  The 182nd Trolls experienced a disastrous raiding attempt in Moussoro and 
sank to Green quality.


  Here is the financial report for Giovanna's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 33 gold in revenue.  16 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  33 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Giovanna was left 
with 27 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Rolando
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I prepared my armies to defend Kajaani and the surrounding 
provinces.
  During early summer, I, responsible for the defense of Kajaani, learned of 
an enemy move on Rejaf.  I marched into Rejaf from Kajaani to defend Rejaf 
against its would-be conquerors.  West of here lies the province of Quantara 
Roo (#1403), ruled by Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  It is said to be 
a Plain province occupied by Humans.  Their Human warriors prefer to array 
themselves as Legion and Heavy Cavalry.

  A great host of savage warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Desert province of Rejaf, 
held by II Kahn (#6).  Guerin (#18) was in command of the invading armies.  
The defenders were led by me.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle 
as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Rejaf (1503):

 124th/S    277th                                                     
 Dragons    Eagles                                                    
