  DEFENDING ARMY

  Guerin commanded a host of loyal soldiers.  I marched with my loyal 
troops, eyes set in grim resolution.  Tiffany stood ready at the head of her 
thousands.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Guerin (#18)'s men, ill-supplied in the tortuous desert 
campaign, suffered from thirst.  Guerin was unlucky this time, for supplies 
were running low and some of his troops had to fight on empty stomachs.  On 
the other hand his clever tactical planning gave his side a clear advantage.

  Out on the right flank, the Elite 240th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 74th 
Camel Corps.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 74th Camel Corps 
and attacked without mercy.  The 240th Skeletal Bowmen fought with the 74th 
Camel Corps and cut them down like beanstalks.
  In the interior front, the Crack 110th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
20th Legion.  The 277th Eagles swooped down on the 20th Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  In this sector, the 20th Legion's opponents were lined up in 
an upslope position.  But the 20th Legion charged them, and because there 
was no counter-charge, the 20th Legion shoved them off the crest and gained 
the upper hand.  In spite of the 20th Legion's good luck, the 110th Bowmen 
fought the 20th Legion and managed to make some measure of progress.
  Within the interior front, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen were inspired 
to fanatiscm by Guerin, their heroic First Elder of Elvenkind.  They faced 
the 21st Legion.  On this battleground, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen were 
slightly disrupted by a slippery patch of ground and they joined the fight 
at a tiny disadvantage.  Even so, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen battled the 21st 
Legion and gradually shoved them back.
  Within the interior lines, the Green 292nd Skeletal Legion were arrayed 
against the 244th Light Cavalry.  Here, the 292nd Skeletal Legion were 
inspired by the exhortations of an officer who bellowed "Do you want to be 
remembered as Heroes or despised as cowards?  Charge!  !  !"  Even with the 
292nd Skeletal Legion's good luck, the 292nd Skeletal Legion fought the 
244th Light Cavalry and were bent back by their pressure.
  Within the interior front, the Crack 241st Skeletal Bowmen faced the 239th 
Legion.  In this engagement, the contest was a straightforward bashing match 
determined by the courage of the men themselves in melee combat.  The 241st 
Skeletal Bowmen fought with the 239th Legion and the fighting here proved 
inconclusive.
  In the interior lines, the 109th Skeletal Heavy Cavalry were inspired to 
berserk fanatiscm by Guerin, their heroic First Elder of Elvenkind.  They 
were arrayed against the 230th Legion.  The Heavy Cavalry troops charged the 
230th Legion and they wavered under the initial impact.  Here, the 230th 
Legion had to go through a ford.  But their enemy attacked before the 
crossing operation was completed.  The 109th Skeletal Heavy Cavalry battled 
with the 230th Legion and steadily advanced against them.
  Out on the left outside flank, the 209th Skeletal Warg Riders were arrayed 
against the 276th Light Cavalry.  The horses of the 276th Light Cavalry were 
spooked by the terrible Beasts they beheld.  On this field, the 276th 
Light Cavalry were held off by earthen ramparts built up by their opponents. 
But the 276th Light Cavalry had a giant worm on retainer to undermine it, 
and the 276th Light Cavalry broke through quickly, demoralizing them.  The 
209th Skeletal Warg Riders battled with the 276th Light Cavalry and were 
slowly bent back by their attack.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Kahn (#6), a final 
savage thrust finished off their enemy and won the day for Guerin (#18).  
The 240th Skeletal Bowmen demolished the 74th Camel Corps.  The 109th 
Skeletal Heavy Cavalry destroyed the 230th Legion.  The 276th Light Cavalry 
slew the 209th Skeletal Warg Riders almost to a man.  The 124th Skeletal 
Dragons pursued the enemy and annihilated the 239th Legion.  The 277th 
Eagles chased after the enemy and scattered the 20th Legion in all 
directions.
  Rejaf was overrun by the forces of Guerin.  I retreated to Kajaani.  
Tiffany made for the safety of Kajaani with her motley army.  Her experience 
raised her skill in Tactics.
  With the advent of the late summer season, the plague struck the 276th 
Light Cavalry in Kajaani and destroyed them.  I really tried hard to improve 
my Tactics, but I practiced in vain.
  The summer surrendered to fall.  I tried to improve my Tactics, but the 
task was beyond my natural aptitude.
  The fall season cooled into a frigid early winter.  I tried to improve my 
Tactics, but the task was beyond my natural aptitude.

  Thy humble servant,   Rolando


From: Hakim
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter gave way to spring, and I made ready to carry out my 
imperial assignments.  Giovanna was resurrected by the spell cast by me.  My 
experience improved my skill in White Magic.
  Windy spring blossomed into a sultry early summer.  Hakim's attempted cast 
of the Phantasmal Armies spell was unsuccessful.
  In late summer, I cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were 
formed for Giovanna.
  With the advent of the fall season I rode into Moussoro.  I marched along 
some previously unexplored paths, raising our exploration knowledge to 100%. 
I encountered no monsters.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  I travelled to Kajaani.  I 
encountered no marauding monsters.

  Thy humble servant,   Hakim


From: Tonto, Squire to Tiffany
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Tiffany prepared her armies to defend Kajaani and the 
surrounding provinces.
  With the advent of the early summer season, Isis failed in her attempt to 
cast an Oratory spell.  Tiffany, responsible for the defense of Kajaani, 
learned of an enemy move on Rejaf.  Tiffany marched into Rejaf from Kajaani 
to defend Rejaf against its would-be conquerors.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer arrived.  The plague 
struck the 244th Light Cavalry in Kajaani and destroyed them.  Tiffany cast 
a Bless spell.  Tigerhome was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless 
affected no armies in Tigerhome.
  With the coming of the fall season Tiffany cast a Bless spell.  Sageleaf 
was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in 
Sageleaf.
  During early winter, Tiffany tried a Bless spell, but botched it.

  Thy humble servant,   Tonto, Squire to Tiffany


From: Moosu, Squire to Drake
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter gave way to spring, and Drake made ready to carry out his 
urgent assignments.  He marched on Pearlgate (#1703) with his command.
  With the advent of the early summer season Drake could not resurrect 
Giovanna's predecessor because Giovanna had already advanced in skill.  So, 
Drake practiced his Necromancy for months, but could make no significant 
progress.
  In late summer, Drake could not resurrect Giovanna's predecessor because 
Giovanna had already advanced in skill.  Instead, Drake practiced his 
Navigation well but could not improve his Navigation.  He conducted military 
maneuvers and the 248th Light Cavalry rose in quality.
  In fall, Drake entered the Monastery to see what special power it might 
possess.
  Drake saw nothing special while scouting out the Monastery.
  With the advent of the early winter season, Drake could not give treasure 
23 to Giovanna because Drake did not own it.

  Thy humble servant,   Moosu, Squire to Drake


From: Watson, Squire to Isis
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, Isis set out to quench her thirst 
for adventure.  She failed in her attempt to cast a Flood spell.
  During early summer, Isis failed in her attempt to cast an Oratory spell.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Isis tried hard to improve her 
Element Magic, but she practiced in vain.
  During fall, Isis rehearsed and practiced her Element Magic and improved 
substantially.
  The fall cooled into the stillness of early winter.  Isis practiced her 
Element Magic diligently for months, but could make no progress.

  Thy humble servant,   Watson, Squire to Isis


From: Bairn
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  My attempted cast of the Flood spell didn't work.
  During early summer, I could not cast a Oratory spell because I had no 
skill in Psychic Magic.  Instead, I practiced my Necromancy well but could 
not improve my skill in Necromancy.
  With the coming of the late summer season, I worked on my Element Magic 
but was thwarted in my efforts.
  During fall, I tried to practice my Element Magic, but the task seemed 
beyond my aptitude.
  The fall season cooled into a frigid early winter.  I was tutored in the 
art of Element Magic by Isis.  I tried to improve my Element Magic, but the 
task seemed beyond my ability.

  Thy humble servant,   Bairn


From: Adhemar
To: Giovanna

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter gave way to spring.  I travelled to the Andrea Doria Sea.  
To the north is a land of glaciers which apparently has no end.  While 
adventuring, I saw no monster.
  With the advent of the early summer season, I journeyed to Elkhome.  West 
of here is San Andreas (#1401), a Sea province ruled by no one, where no 
races dwell.  To the north, the landscape is scarred by a broad expanse of 
ice.  I discovered a feature in Elkhome: a Glade (#91) occupied by 
the Centaur.  Legend says the Large Hoard of Gold is hidden here.  
Wood-Elves say that the Centaur is a cross-breed, with the body of a man and 
the trunk and legs of a horse.  He is a good archer and is usually friendly. 
During my travels this season, a Centaur unexpectedly came at me from out of 
nowhere.  I hailed the Centaur with friendly words, and a fight was avoided.

  In late summer, I wandered freely about Elkhome, uncovering its mysteries, 
and raising our exploration level in Elkhome to 68%.  I also discovered a 
Hollow Tree (#35) in Elkhome, occupied by the Treant.  Legend says the Huge 
Hoard of Gold is hidden here.  The Treant is a large tree capable of moving 
its limbs and arms much as a man does.  While adventuring, I saw no 
monsters.
  The summer surrendered to fall.  I explored Elkhome, taking precise notes 
of the terrain and features, and now 100% of it has been explored.  During 
my travels this season, I encountered a Black Dragon.  But I hailed 
the Black Dragon with friendly words, and combat was averted.

  With the advent of the early winter season, I moved into Damnonia.  To the 
west there lies a Forest province known as Sherwood (#1302), a rich land of 
Humans where II Kahn rules.  Their Human warriors prefer to array themselves 
in the style of Legion and Light Cavalry.  I was informed by some peasants 
of a perilous feature in Damnonia, a Tomb (#80) inhabited by the Ice Devil.  
What treasure may lie there is unknown.  Legend has it that the Ice Devil is 
an extraordinarily cruel, cold and very powerful devil with magical powers.  
I located a previously unheard of Cave (#110) in Damnonia, inhabited by 
the Black Dragon.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  The Black Dragon 
is an Evil and very powerful acid-spitting dragon.  I saw no monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Adhemar


